% === provenance: PythonTimeComplexity ===
% CLAIM: Looking up a key in a dictionary, or testing membership in a set,
%   takes constant time on average, while the same test in a list takes
%   time proportional to the list's length; and removing an element from
%   the front of a list is linear, whereas a deque does it in constant
%   time.
% FOUND-VIA (here): known-item, primary source.  A performance claim about
%   CPython's containers is answered by CPython's own documented
%   complexities, not by a literature search.  The provenance block is
%   copied from modules/containers/slides-sets-stacks-queues/ltnotes.bib;
%   this deck cites it in \cref{sec:epost,sec:banken,sec:cowsay}.
% PICKED: the Python wiki's TimeComplexity page is the project's own
%   tabulation; the alternative -- timing the operations -- would measure
%   one machine rather than the data structure.
% QUOTE: "This page documents the time-complexity (aka 'Big O' or 'Big
%   Oh') of various operations in current CPython."  From the list table:
%   "Get Item O(1)", "Insert O(n)", "Delete Item O(n)" and "x in s O(n)"
%   (average and amortized worst case alike).  From the set table,
%   "x in s" is O(1) average and O(n) worst case.  From the dict table,
%   "Get Item" is O(1) average and O(n) amortized worst case.  From the
%   collections.deque table, "Append", "Pop", "Appendleft" and "Popleft"
%   are all O(1).
% VERIFIED (here): full text of https://wiki.python.org/moin/TimeComplexity
%   read 2026-09-03; the four tables (list, set, dict, collections.deque)
%   carry the figures quoted.  Honest limitation: the page states it
%   documents "current CPython" and gives average cases, so the material
%   states the claim with that qualification.  NOT re-fetched for this
%   deck.
% COUNTER: not applicable in the literature sense; the qualification the
%   page itself carries (CPython, average case, amortized worst case) is
%   the counter-consideration, and it is reproduced in the material.
% DATE: 2026-09-03
@online{PythonTimeComplexity,
  author       = {{Python Software Foundation}},
  title        = {TimeComplexity},
  subtitle     = {Python Wiki},
  url          = {https://wiki.python.org/moin/TimeComplexity},
  urldate      = {2026-09-03},
  year         = {2026},
}


